Modified 2026-11-05. Summary of changes from the original:

- Merge policy: auto-merge is off by default; approved PRs are handed to a
  human (label factory:approved). When enabled, auto-merge is capped by risk
  and merges only the exact gated commit (--match-head-commit).
- Script-enforced escalation: changes to CI, infrastructure, dependency
  manifests, migrations and agent instructions always go to a human.
- New factory/bin/guard: a PreToolUse hook on every agent that checks file
  writes per role and blocks common forms of secret reads, GitHub writes,
  unsafe pushes and writes into the factory itself; read-only roles get an
  allowlisted shell.
- Draft PRs are opened by factory/bin/job instead of the builder, so no
  LLM-written title passes through a shell.
- The gate runs checks.sh with a scrubbed environment and a time limit, and
  protected paths now include added files and the factory's own files.
- Issue authors must have triage or write access by default.
- Per-job cost ceiling, per-job audit trail (events.jsonl), single global lock
  (removes a deadlock), cost accounting that can't block state changes,
  corrected prices, models governed from config.json.
- New factory/bin/doctor preflight, a unit and pipeline test suite, a hardened
  dashboard (Content-Security-Policy, localhost-only instructions).
- Lite and full profiles chosen by risk; intake works to a size budget and
  writes acceptance criteria; the gate records each change's size; a
  benchmark protocol and `job metrics` CSV export.
- Fail-closed check that the agents' guard hooks actually ran, and preflight
  checks for folder trust and organization hook policy.
- Documentation rewritten; promotional material, marketing links, images and
  third-party usernames removed.

Further modified 2026-11-06:

- The guard parses shell commands the way bash does and ties every write to a
  job in the agent's own stage; an adversarial regression corpus covers it.
- A control-file seal: job commands and the gate refuse after the factory's
  own files, git config or git hooks change mid-run.
- Text bound for GitHub is filtered for credentials and images and capped.
- The preflight fails on a GitHub token with the classic `repo` scope and
  explains which risks auto-merge covers.
- Dependency changes wait for a human before any check runs them; jobs can be
  cancelled and the factory paused; retried steps don't post twice.
- Reviewers and the approver get a read-only shell; the orchestrator reads job
  files through a filter that frames them as data.
- CI, tests for every job transition, a runbook, a security policy and a
  changelog; the builder's stop hook is removed and transcript costs are
  cached.

Further modified 2026-11-07:

- The gate's verdict is posted as a commit status, and unattended merges wait
  for the repository's CI.
- Routing follows the diff: sensitive paths add the security review.
- Optional GitHub App identity with short-lived tokens.
- A runtime container with an egress firewall; the factory pushes, agents
  don't.
- A hash-chained audit log, and a pilot kit.

